--
N5008 [dcl.fct.default]/1,4: the default argument on the first declaration
of a function template applies to calls that follow its definition, which
redeclares it without the default.  The definition replaced the
declaration and lost it ("found no match for symbol 'f'"; inside the
template g the body was dropped).  A namespace member defined
by a qualified name (`n::h', [dcl.meaning.general]/3.1) was never merged
with its declaration at all, default or not.  test_member.desc
covers a member function template defined outside its class.  libstdc++ 13's vformat_to
calls __format::__do_vformat_to with three arguments, so its bodies
(format:3759/3765) were dropped in every program including <format>.
bin53: CONVERSION ERROR.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program
(-std=c++98), and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
